some command

mariadb -u root -p - Connect to the server as root.
mariadb -u user -p -h host_ip - Connect to a specific host IP address.
sudo mariadb - Log in automatically using Unix socket authentication.
mariadb-dump -u user -p db_name > backup.sql - Export data to a backup file.
mariadb-admin -u root -p status - Check the runtime status of the server.

SHOW DATABASES; - View all databases on the server.
CREATE DATABASE db_name; - Create a completely new database.
USE db_name; - Select a database to make it active.
DROP DATABASE db_name; - Permanently delete an entire database.

SHOW TABLES; - List all existing tables within the active database.
CREATE TABLE table_name (col1 INT, col2 VARCHAR(50)); - Create a table with defined columns.DESCRIBE table_name; - View the columns, data types, and primary keys of a table.
ALTER TABLE table_name ADD col_name DATATYPE; - Modify a table structure by adding a column.
DROP TABLE table_name; - Permanently remove a table and its data.Data Manipulation Commands (DML)Use these commands to read, insert, update, and delete data rows:SELECT * FROM table_name; - Retrieve all records from a table.
INSERT INTO table_name (col1, col2) VALUES (val1, val2); - Insert new records.
UPDATE table_name SET col1 = val1 WHERE condition; - Edit records matching a specific rule.

DELETE FROM table_name WHERE condition; - Erase rows matching a specific condition.User & Permission ManagementControl database security, user access, and system permissions:CREATE USER 'username'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'password'; - Set up a local user account.
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON db_name.* TO 'username'@'localhost'; - Assign permissions to a user.
SHOW GRANTS FOR 'username'@'localhost'; - Display all permissions given to a user.
REVOKE ALL PRIVILEGES ON db_name.* FROM 'username'@'localhost'; - Strip user permissions.DROP USER 'username'@'localhost'; - Erase a user account from the server.Diagnostics & Exit CommandsMonitor current operations or disconnect safely:SHOW PROCESSLIST; - Show active client connections and active operations.SHOW STATUS; - View current performance metrics and traffic.EXIT; - Safely disconnect from the database shell prompt.
